---
date added: 2026-10-26
title: Sheet-Pan Thanksgiving Stuffing
author: Yossy Arefi
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/792771373-sheet-pan-thanksgiving-stuffing
tags: stuffing, thanksgiving, sheet pan, side dish, make-ahead
servings: 10
time required: 55 minutes
cook time: 40 minutes
---

Heat oven to 400 degrees with a rack set in the center.

Tear the @crusty bread{1%large loaf} (like white, whole wheat or sourdough, about 1¼ pounds) into roughly 2-inch pieces and place in a single layer on a large rimmed #baking sheet{}. Bake the bread until dry to the touch but not browned, ~{5-10%minutes}. Set bread aside but keep the oven on.

In a large #skillet{} over medium, melt 6 tablespoons of the @unsalted butter{8%tablespoons} (divided, plus more for the pan) and add the @celery stalks{5} (diced, about 2 cups), @yellow onion{1%large} (diced, about 2 cups) and @green apple{1%cup} (diced, from about 1 apple), along with the @kosher salt{1 1/2%teaspoons} (such as Diamond Crystal) and @black pepper{1/2%teaspoon}. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are soft and translucent, ~{7-10%minutes}. Add the @fresh sage{2%tablespoons} (finely chopped) and @fresh thyme leaves{1%tablespoon} and cook for ~{1%minute} more.

In a medium #bowl{} or liquid measuring cup, whisk the @large eggs{2} into the @chicken or vegetable broth{2 1/2%cups} until well combined.

Transfer the bread to a large #bowl{} and add the cooked vegetables and @fresh parsley{1/2%cup} (roughly chopped). Stir to combine, then add the broth mixture and stir until the bread is moistened and no liquid remains in the bottom of the bowl.

Butter the baking sheet used to dry out the bread, then add the stuffing mixture and spread into an even layer. Dot the top with the remaining 2 tablespoons of butter.

Bake until golden brown and crisp, ~{35-45%minutes}. Serve warm. (Stuffing can be made ahead and kept at room temperature for several hours. Reheat at 350 degrees until warmed through.)
